    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Ncux17Yj6ANSAph5xngrN3)_\n\nFollow-up to #60 (merged).\n\n## What changes\n- With `sp-tag-emoji-mode` on, `vulpea-select-describe-fn` is `sp-tag-emoji-describe-note`: the emoji of the note's tags, then the title (`vulpea-select`, `vulpea-find`, `vulpea-insert`). It depends on the note alone, so vulpea's candidate cache stays valid; the previous value (now `vulpea-select-describe-outline-full` from `sp-vulpea-base`) is restored when the mode is turned off.\n- `sp-select-note` is my own selector (same keywords as `vulpea-select`) built on `vulpea-select-from`: the tags in a column at the right edge (`(space :align-to (- right N))`, `N` a fraction of the frame width), small and dimmed, still matchable.\n- `sp-insert-note` is `vulpea-insert` with the same emoji and tag column; the link text stays the plain title.\n- Both bypass vulpea's candidate cache while they run (the column width is not a property of the note).\n- **Callers now use them**, for one look everywhere: `sp-org-create-note-and-link` (its \"insert existing\" branch) and the wikilink conversion, `sp-tab-inbox`, `sp-move-region-to-heading`, the graph start note in `sp-graphs`, and `sp-collec-query-select-note` (which also no longer confuses same-titled notes). Each of those modules now requires `sp-tag-emoji`.\n- Rules can opt out of the selector with `:select nil`. `sp-tag-emoji-select-visit` is not part of this PR.\n- Docs and CHANGELOG follow.\n\n## Worth checking\n`sp-org-create-note-and-link` used to call `vulpea-insert` with two positional functions. Upstream `vulpea-insert` takes keywords (`:filter-fn`, `:create-fn`), so the call now uses keywords; if your installed vulpea still has the positional signature, that call needs to go back.\n\n## Checked (Emacs 29.3, headless)\nCandidate strings with a stubbed `vulpea-select-from` and fake notes, `sp-insert-note` calling a stubbed `vulpea-insert` with the emoji describe function and the cache off, mode on/off restoring the describe function; every changed `.el` reads and balances, and each tangles from its doc.\n\n## Not checked\nThe look in a real minibuffer (Vertico / mini-frame), the callers with a real vulpea database, and the real `vulpea-insert` signature (read from upstream source, not your installed copy).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Xrgdre7xkfaqJ3bbVqXTo5",
